title: Breast cancer screening and prevention
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Risk assessment:'' Gail informs medication counseling; family-history models such as Tyrer-Cuzick guide MRI eligibility.
** Age ≥35 with Gail five-year risk ≥1.7% supports individualized medication discussion.
** Lifetime risk ≥20%: annual MRI plus mammography; inherited risk requires gene-specific starting ages.
** Chest irradiation at 10–30: begin both eight years later, never before 25.
* ''Average risk:'' Mammography from 40: annually per NCCN; biennially through 74 per USPSTF.
** Balance mortality benefit against false positives and overdiagnosis.
** Extremely dense breasts: NCCN recommends MRI from 50; consider 40, with uncertain interval.
* ''Biopsy:'' Usually excise atypical ductal hyperplasia; observe selected concordant atypical lobular hyperplasia/classic LCIS.
** LCIS means lobular carcinoma in situ; discordance or nonclassic variants require further evaluation.
* ''Medication:'' Elevated-risk women: tamoxifen before/after menopause; raloxifene or off-label aromatase inhibitors only postmenopausally.
** Prevent estrogen-receptor-positive cancers; weigh tamoxifen’s uterine/thrombotic risks, raloxifene’s thrombosis, and aromatase-inhibitor bone loss.
** Low-dose tamoxifen: placebo-controlled intraepithelial-neoplasia evidence; alternative when standard dosing is unacceptable.
* ''High-penetrance variants:'' Discuss bilateral mastectomy; residual risk persists. See [[Cancer genetics]].
** After childbearing, salpingo-oophorectomy: BRCA1 at 35–40, BRCA2 at 40–45; principally ovarian-risk reduction.
** Peritoneal risk persists; breast protection from salpingo-oophorectomy is uncertain.
* Encourage exercise, healthy weight, and less alcohol; supplements lack proven prevention benefit.

Sources: ASCO SEP 2026, ch.10 “Breast Cancer,” pp.435–440, Fig.10-1; NCCN Breast Cancer Screening and Diagnosis v1.2026, BSCR-1–4, Discussion MS-13–17; NCCN Breast Cancer Risk Reduction v1.2026, BRISK-B, Discussion MS-17–18; NCCN Genetic/Familial High-Risk Assessment: Breast, Ovarian, Pancreatic, and Prostate v1.2027, BRCA-A 2, Discussion MS-24–25; [[USPSTF 2024|https://www.uspreventiveservicestaskforce.org/uspstf/document/ClinicalSummaryFinal/breast-cancer-screening]].
